ttps://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/deployments","created_at":"2022-11-09T03:00:19Z","updated_at":"2026-09-17T19:31:24Z","pushed_at":"2026-09-17T19:31:22Z","git_url":"git://github.com/rrnewton/hermit.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:rrnewton/hermit.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit","homepage":null,"size":247745,"stargazers_count":1,"watchers_count":1,"language":"Rust","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":true,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":0,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":562,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":0,"open_issues":562,"watchers":1,"default_branch":"main"}},"_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/3073"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3073"},"issue":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/3073"},"comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/3073/comments"},"review_comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/3073/comments"},"review_comment":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/comments{/number}"},"commits":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/3073/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/statuses/62cb9321b8c95cf184904d98cf03677fcbe8f2fb"}},"author_association":"OWNER","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/3070","id":4560197953,"node_id":"PR_kwDOIZiOrM8AAAABD88ZQQ","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3070","diff_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3070.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3070.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/3070","number":3070,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Carry a scorecard write-back refusal's own words into the durable record","user":{"login":"rrnewton","id":274582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDU4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"[hermit2, review-3066, unresolved, devbig014, role=impl]\n\nPlain Language Summary and Project Impact\n\nA compatibility scorecard write-back refused, the run handle recorded\n`refused with exit status: 2`, and that number is all any later reader got. The\ntool's explanation existed the whole time -- it went to the run log, which\nnothing joins to the handle -- so the record could not distinguish a genuine\ndata refusal from calling the tool wrong.\n\nThat cost a day. Six validation checkouts are retained on this exact error\ntoday, and diagnosing them meant reading a 540 KB run log to find one line. My\nown first reading of the exit code was wrong for precisely this reason: I\nreproduced exit 2 by invoking the tool without `--results` and was about to\nreport a missing-argument bug. The real cause, recoverable only from the log,\nis a parity-history candidate-identity change on one KVM cell.\n\nTask: scorecard_write_back_refusal\n\n`local_scorecard_writeback` ran the tool with `.status()`, which INHERITS the\nchild's streams, so nothing was ever available to record. It now uses\n`.output()`, re-emits both streams verbatim first -- keeping the child's words\nin the run log, which is the only reason they were recoverable at all -- and\nfolds them into the error beside the status.\n\nFour decisions in `refusal_detail`, each because the obvious alternative is a\nsmaller version of the same defect:\n\n* stderr preferred, stdout as fallback, and the stream is NAMED. A tool that\n  explains itself on the wrong stream is still explaining itself.\n* A tool that refuses and says nothing produces\n  \"the tool refused without writing any explanation\" rather than an empty\n  field. Silence is a finding; an empty field reads as unset.\n* Truncation is STATED with the true byte count. A silently shortened cause is\n  this defect one size down.\n* The TAIL is kept, because a refusal is what a tool says last. The first\n  implementation kept a one-character tail and the test caught it.\n\nThe bound is 4096 bytes, sized from measurement rather than taste: the refusal\nthat stranded seven hours of validation was a single 317-byte line.\n\nNOT CHANGED, and deliberately. The refusal is genuine data, so this does not\nmake it pass. And I did not change what a failed write-back does to cleanup --\nretaining the checkout is what converts a one-cell disagreement into a\nfleet-wide outage, but retaining unconsumed evidence is a safety property and\nrelaxing it to clear an outage is a goalpost move. It needs an owner decision,\nand it is recorded on the task rather than taken here.\n\nDeterminism\n\nA pure function of the child's bytes: no clock, no ordering, no host state. The\ntool is invoked with the same arguments in the same directory; only the capture\nmode changed, and both streams are re-emitted so the run log is unchanged.\n\nLinux Semantics\n\nNo guest syscall, process, signal or exit-status behaviour is affected.\n\nValidation\n\nThe rust-script suite for scripts/validate.rs: 79 passed / 5 failed, against\n73 passed / 5 failed at pristine on this same head. Identical failure set --\nthose five are pre-existing and none is this change's -- and the six extra\npasses are the six tests added here. cargo fmt --all --check clean.\n\nThe primary test uses the REAL 317-byte refusal from run 1838's log verbatim,\nand asserts the record now names both the cell and the kind of disagreement.\n\nMeasured in both directions, four controls:\n\n  silence returns an empty string        -> the silence test fails\n  truncation keeps the head              -> \"the tail was dropped\"\n  revert to .status()                    -> does not compile, no stderr to read\n  drop refusal_detail from the call site -> the call-site test fails with\n                                            \"refused with exit status: 2: \"\n                                            and nothing after the colon\n\n⚠️ THAT LAST CONTROL IS WHY THERE IS A CALL-SITE TEST AT ALL. Run against the\nfirst five tests it PASSED -- they exercise the helper directly and prove\nnothing about whether it is wired in. That is the third instance in one day of\na check that reports a binding it never established, so the sixth test drives\nthe real function against a real refusing child, with a succeeding child and the\nnested/off-the-record gates as controls in the other direction.\n","created_at":"2026-09-17T15:28:09Z","updated_at":"2026-09-17T16:00:39Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"e07f0f993b5927e706339ec50df415a4d52430ac","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/3070/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/3070/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/3070/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/statuses/cb7077228cb3308a1e2594d43add36100bab2232","head":{"label":"rrnewton:review-3066/scorecard-refusal-carries-its-cause","ref":"review-3066/scorecard-refusal-carries-its-cause","sha":"cb7077228cb3308a1e2594d43add36100bab2232","user":{"login":"rrnewton","id":274582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDU4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":563646124,"node_id":"R_kgDOIZiOrA","name":"hermit","full_name":"rrnewton/hermit","private":false,"owner":{"login":"rrnewton","id":274582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDU4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit","description":"Hermit launches linux x86_64 programs in a special, hermetically isolated sandbox to control their execution. Hermit translates normal, nondeterministic behavior, into deterministic, repeatable behavior. This can be used for various applications, including replay-debugging, reproducible artifacts, chaos mode concurrency testing and bug analysis.","fork":true,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit","forks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/forks","keys_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/keys{/key_id}","collaborators_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/collaborators{/collaborator}","teams_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/teams","hooks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/hooks","issue_events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/events{/number}","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/events","assignees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/assignees{/user}","branches_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/branches{/branch}","tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/tags","blobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/git/blobs{/sha}","git_tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/git/tags{/sha}","git_refs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/git/refs{/sha}","trees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/git/trees{/sha}","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/statuses/{sha}","languages_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/languages","stargazers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/stargazers","contributors_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/r