n/hermit/pulls/3066/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/statuses/b27530786ae57fb9cc43d9d49563ce8f02e64013"}},"author_association":"OWNER","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/3030","id":4548734409,"node_id":"PR_kwDOIZiOrM8AAAABDyAtyQ","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3030","diff_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3030.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3030.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/3030","number":3030,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Run default compatibility checks in the pinned image","user":{"login":"rrnewton","id":274582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDU4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"[hermit2, degraded-dev-hermit, gpt-6-astra, devbig014, role=impl]\n\n## Plain Language Summary and Project Impact\n\nThe 189 default portable compatibility commands currently run against host tools. Route those commands and their fixture producer through the pinned image, preserving every original payload, budget and result oracle. Give the image fixture an explicit pinned-toolchain mode and separate run-state directory so mixed host/image selections cannot overwrite each other's fixtures.\n\nTask: hermetic-validate-v3-clean-base-minimal-env-fixed-test-workdir\n\nThe image declares 153 executable paths, adds 19 links to locked package outputs and preserves the existing toolchain. Manifest syntax, duplicate/empty declarations and unavailable providers refuse. All 189 hosted counterparts and their 206-node closure remain unchanged. The image digest is `sha256:715ac8c96ef1267fb59f531d9885b91d5e1d5dfbb43126551187d7f6fb4ac633`; no Nix input or dependency pin was upgraded.\n\n## Validation and review\n\n- Focused Rust generator/selection controls, package all-target Clippy, workspace formatting, Python wrapper/cache controls and Nix positive/refusal controls passed on the exact committed source blobs.\n- Normal image build passed in 187.486s under 4 CPU/12GiB/zero swap. It reached the memory cap (76107 max events) with zero OOM/kill events; this is assembly evidence, not spare-memory headroom.\n- The actual image passed 153 declared-path and 140 PATH-command checks. A fresh read-only OLD8157 probe directly matched all 88 retained providers' resolved paths, modes, sizes and SHA256 against NEW715a in 1.443s, with no host mount over /nix.\n- Five actual fixture invocations passed: host/image sequential, host/image concurrent with measured overlap, and image recreation. Host bytes/inodes/mtimes remained unchanged. These were fixture controls with zero Hermit invocations.\n- Root native and independent Claude source reviews approve tree `b7f349b09b8be7c6a88e80c300651706203736d7`, exactly committed as `934032fab5bcdde908bccdee6fd99effc6f15c35`. Claude's initially unresolved old-provider hash provenance was subsequently resolved by the fresh 88-entry probe and independent root readback. Optional source observations remain documented; no review marker is synthesized.\n\n- Normal verified push passed changed-Rust formatting and the actual `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` hook. The whole hook/push operation took 89.446s under 4 CPU/8GiB/zero swap/1024tasks; no standalone Clippy-duration claim. Fresh remote readback confirms all nine blobs/modes and exact commit 934032fa.\n\n## Draft limits\n\nActual compatibility execution is pending. No full validation receipt or dependency-completeness credit is claimed. The original commands retain strict mode with legacy stripped verification (ptrace backend, default log level); this change makes no L2/bitwise-parity claim. No comparator, test assertion, node budget or workload case was weakened.\n\nThis is one part of the all-family hermetic task: full still has 32 unwrapped nodes and super 144. The task remains open. The proposed nine-node focused official-driver run is separately held for controller review and disk admission; the 211-node closure has not run. Detailed command/status/source-bound artifacts remain under the coordinator's `ignored/ci-hub/hermetic-v3-dev-hermit-20260916/` evidence tree.\n","created_at":"2026-09-16T14:29:39Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T14:29:39Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/3030/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/3030/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/3030/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/statuses/934032fab5bcdde908bccdee6fd99effc6f15c35","head":{"label":"rrnewton:dev-hermit/hermetic-v3-ready-20260916","ref":"dev-hermit/hermetic-v3-ready-20260916","sha":"934032fab5bcdde908bccdee6fd99effc6f15c35","user":{"login":"rrnewton","id":274582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDU4Mg==","