king":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":0,"open_issues":562,"watchers":1,"default_branch":"main"}},"_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/3009"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3009"},"issue":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/3009"},"comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/3009/comments"},"review_comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/3009/comments"},"review_comment":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/comments{/number}"},"commits":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/3009/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/statuses/e26c832e98e23eff3044c874467c0a991827c20f"}},"author_association":"OWNER","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/2969","id":4456821807,"node_id":"PR_kwDOIZiOrM8AAAABCaW0Lw","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/2969","diff_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/2969.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/2969.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/2969","number":2969,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Use harness-managed run evidence for verification","user":{"login":"rrnewton","id":274582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDU4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"[hermit2, mega-lander, unresolved, devbig014, role=impl]\n\n## Plain Language Summary and Project Impact\n\nThis cuts ptrace, KVM, and LiteInst verification cells over from Hermit's internal two-run mode to two ordinary `hermit run --run-evidence-dir` processes managed by the manifest harness. The runs are independently schedulable under the existing global process cap, publish typed evidence, and are compared in-process with `BitwiseInfoV1`. A successful cell retains exactly run 1's canonical log as a verified deterministic gzip plus typed descriptor and outer-ledger binding, then removes both raw logs.\n\nBefore this change, these cells delegated pair ownership and comparison to the CLI's internal verifier. After it, the harness owns process scheduling, evidence validation, comparison, retention, restart accounting, and failure classification while public `hermit run` behavior remains unchanged unless the new harness-only flags are selected.\n\nTask: `flip-verify-to-two-harness-managed-runs-with-retained-logs`\n\n## Determinism\n\nEach pair shares one immutable prepared guest but has distinct no-clobber work, capture, result, stdout, stderr, and evidence paths. The harness waits for both terminal processes, then accepts only complete typed sidecars with nonzero canonical INFO records and matching size/digest metadata. Missing, empty, truncated, malformed, unreadable, replaced, aliased, or digest-mismatched evidence yields `no_result`, never success. `BitwiseInfoV1` removes only the real wall-clock prefix and ordinalizes host addresses; all remaining INFO payload bytes and guest status/stdout/stderr are exact.\n\nRetry remains restricted to the existing typed `ProductFailure` rule and repeats a complete pair. Retention recomputes compressed and uncompressed bytes, sizes, and digests, publishes exactly one run-1 gzip and descriptor durably, binds it into schema-10 outer history, and removes the two raw canonical logs only after publication.\n\n## Linux Semantics\n\nThe default CLI, public `--log-file`, exit codes, and ordinary guest descriptors are unchanged. The discoverable harness-only `--run-result-json`, `--guest-stdout`, and `--guest-stderr` options require `--run-evidence-dir` and use unique no-clobber regular files held relative to the claimed directory. Ptrace and LiteInst install those preopened guest descriptors after Reverie's container setup so Hermit's own diagnostics remain separate; controls cover stdout/stderr/status, descriptor behavior, session/process-group identity, aliasing, and path replacement.\n\nSaBRe intentionally remains on its named legacy internal-verifier path because its plugin DETLOG is available only through shared stderr. DBT remains absent/prelaunch-refused because its current evidence-file mechanism implies isolated process groups and would change guest `setsid`/`setpgid` behavior. Neither path is presented as equivalent.\n\n## Relationship to gVisor\n\nNo gVisor or KVM execution semantics change. KVM uses the same typed sidecar and canonical comparison contract, but guest output is copied from the existing virtual-console result and the report continues to state the existing exit-code-only disposition limitation; it does not invent signal precision.\n\n## Validation\n\nExact head: `e7af5cd8e5a80a0b74be5f44f26b33d4798c2697`, stacked on PR #2968 exact head `841fe4f6857c19f4e3bcfe135fb2601da2c8f925`.\n\n- `cargo test -p hermit-manifest-plan --all-targets`: 277 passed.\n- `cargo test -p hermit --bin hermit`: 240 passed.\n- `cargo test -p hermit --test run_evidence`: 10 passed.\n- `rustup run nightly rust-script --test scripts/validate.rs`: 47 passed.\n- `with-proxy rustup run nightly rust-script scripts/validate.rs --self-test`: passed in a clean clone at the exact head; 12/259 constructed self-test steps selected, 259-node fused plan, expected zero real DAG nodes.\n- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`: passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p hermit -p hermit-manifest-plan --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.\n- Ptrace `c-programs/session-identity`: L2 `BitwiseInfoV1` pass, 128/128 INFO, status 0, no relaxations.\n- LiteInst `c-programs/name-to-handle-regular-eopnotsupp`: L2 `BitwiseInfoV1` pass, 1144/1144 INFO, status 0, no relaxations; guest stdout/stderr remained separate from Hermit diagnostics.\n- KVM `c-programs/session-identity`: L2 `BitwiseInfoV1` pass, 118/118 INFO, status 0, no relaxations, subject to the named KVM disposition limitation above.\n- Each exact-head real control retained exactly one run-1 gzip and no raw canonical log.\n\nThe broader `cargo test -p hermit --all-targets` still has the pre-existing `record_replay_stable_arbitrary_binaries` gettimeofday-policy refusal. The identical command fails at untouched base `841fe4f` on the same host in the same way; this patch does not weaken that policy.\n\nOne first clean-clone self-test attempt hit a transient rustc/LLVM 23.1 SIGSEGV during codegen. It was not an OOM and did not reproduce: an unchanged feature retry, the untouched-base control, and the exact committed-head self-test all passed with the same toolchain/default jobs.\n","created_at":"2026-09-06T15:12:33Z","updated_at":"2026-09-13T10:54:17Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/2969/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/2969/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/2969/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/statuses/e7af5cd8e5a80a0b74be5f44f26b33d4798c2697","head":{"label":"rrnewton:feature/harness-managed-run-evidence-v1","ref":"feature/harness-managed-run-evidence-v1","sha":"e7af5cd8e5a80a0b74be5f44f26b33d4798c2697","user":{"login":"rrnewton","id":274582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDU4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":563646124,"node_id":"R_kgDOIZiOrA","name":"hermit","full_name":"rrnewton/hermit","private":false,"owner":{"login":"rrnewton","id":274582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDU4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subs