on/hermit/statuses/f18b76cc464a3f8f7704f2d7abdbf53baff157e0"}},"author_association":"OWNER","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/2922","id":4417591041,"node_id":"PR_kwDOIZiOrM8AAAABB08XAQ","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/2922","diff_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/2922.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/2922.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/2922","number":2922,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Retain exact validation test results","user":{"login":"rrnewton","id":274582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDU4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"[hermit2, lander-2, unresolved, devbig014, role=impl]\n\n## Plain Language Summary and Project Impact\n\nFull validation currently records aggregate test totals after the producer-owned per-test files have been deleted. This change retains the terminal result and retry count for every counted test as canonical content-addressed evidence, keeps direct compatibility results in their existing separate population, and binds the checked totals and artifact digest into the typed validation ledger row. Missing, malformed, duplicated, count-only, or inconsistent evidence now prevents a schema-8 receipt instead of leaving totals that cannot be independently recomputed.\n\nIt also corrects the stale-base refusal text without weakening admission. A stale head is still refused because it omits main changes available at launch; the message now accurately distinguishes exact-commit validation evidence from the separate hard-green or soft-green decision made at the landing boundary.\n\nTasks: `retain_exact_per_test`, `correct_hermit_validate_stale`\n\n## Determinism\n\nThe artifact is serialized from producer-owned terminal results only. Nodes and per-producer test identities are sorted before serialization, the bytes end in exactly one newline, and SHA-256 binds those canonical bytes to the ledger evidence. Checked recomputation sums each selected terminal node plus the separate compatibility population exactly once. Older outer attempts are excluded only by the existing terminal-attempt selection.\n\nNo runtime or guest-visible behavior changes.\n\n## Linux Semantics\n\nNo Linux syscall, scheduling, filesystem, or process semantics change. This affects validation evidence retention and one admission diagnostic only.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `rust-script --force scripts/validate.rs --self-test` — PASS at `cefe94340d721d537f7afc9398eaa5a2285740a4`; `FINAL_VALIDATE_STATUS PASSED`; 2m11s. This covers canonical 4/3/7 recomputation; terminal-attempt selection; count-only, missing, no-result, duplicate, truncated, corrupt-digest, and spoofed-total refusal; and stale-base refusal with the corrected wording.\n- `cargo test -p hermit-manifest-plan` — PASS, all 205 tests across targets.\n- `cargo check -p hermit-manifest-plan` — PASS.\n- `cargo clippy -p hermit-manifest-plan --all-targets -- -D warnings` — PASS.\n- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` — PASS.\n\nAssurance: L0 infrastructure validation. Backend: none; log level: default; relaxations: none.\n\n## Consumers\n\n- `scripts/validate.rs` selects established terminal attempts, retains the canonical artifact, emits schema 8 only when evidence is complete, and serializes the typed ledger evidence.\n- `ci/manifest-plan/src/ledger.rs::HistoryRow` is the shared typed producer/reader boundary for the new evidence.\n- `compat_test_results` remains the producer for the separate `compatibility` population.\n- `run_test_counts` remains the aggregate whose totals are checked against recomputation.\n- `validate`'s isolated clean-checkout self-test copies and stages both the new module and the modified ledger type, so nested compilation exercises the real files.\n- Downstream receipt and landing readers consume the complete ledger row; their schema-8 verification is intentionally a dependent change rather than inferred in this producer patch.\n","created_at":"2026-09-02T00:44:27Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T01:35:31Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/2922/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/2922/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/2922/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/statuses/cefe94340d721d537f7afc9398eaa5a2285740a4","head":{"label":"rrnewton:fix/retain-exact-per-test-receipt","ref":"fix/retain-exact-per-test-receipt","sha":"cefe94340d721d537f7afc9398eaa5a2285740a4","user":{"login":"rrnewton","id":274582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDU4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":563646124,"node_id":"R_kgDOIZiOrA","name":"hermit","full_name":"rrnewton/hermit","private":false,"owner":{"login":"rrnewton","id":274582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDU4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit","description":"Hermit launches linux x86_64 programs in a special, hermetically isolated sandbox to control their execution. Hermit translates normal, nondeterministic behavior, into deterministic, repeatable behavior. This can be used for va