"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":0,"open_issues":562,"watchers":1,"default_branch":"main"}},"_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/2922"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/2922"},"issue":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/2922"},"comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/2922/comments"},"review_comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/2922/comments"},"review_comment":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/comments{/number}"},"commits":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/2922/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/statuses/cefe94340d721d537f7afc9398eaa5a2285740a4"}},"author_association":"OWNER","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/2907","id":4407148239,"node_id":"PR_kwDOIZiOrM8AAAABBq--zw","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/2907","diff_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/2907.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/2907.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/2907","number":2907,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"demos: derive Demo 8's crash seed, and make a stale one say so","user":{"login":"rrnewton","id":274582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDU4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"[hermit2, demo08review, unresolved, devbig014, role=impl]\n\n## Plain Language Summary and Project Impact\n\nDemo 8 demonstrates Hermit's headline capability on a real program: chaos scheduling finds a use-after-free in `btrfs-convert` that blind execution misses, and replays it. It worked only for someone who already knew a crashing seed. Every seed recorded in the tree was wrong at the current head, the calibration that would have derived a fresh one **could not run at all**, and a stale seed reported itself as a regression in the fix.\n\n**Before:** a reader with a clean tree got either `SKIPPED`, or exit 1 claiming the bug did not reproduce.\n**After:** one command derives a seed for the inputs actually present and prints the ASAN report; a stale record is named as stale and re-derived rather than blamed on the fixture.\n\nBase is `move-demos-directory-into-hermit` (PR #2904), not `main`, because Demo 8 does not exist on `main`. Follow-up to the independent review of that PR — verdict at https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/2904#issuecomment-5485325069.\n\n⚠️ **This PR carries no `Demo-Green-Review` trailer, deliberately.** I performed the review that produced these findings, so I do not certify that my own fix meets them. A separate lane owns that. The commit was made with `HERMIT_DEMO_REVIEW_OVERRIDE=1`, the documented pre-review path, which does not exempt the merge.\n\n## What was broken\n\n**1. Calibration could not run.** `scripts/hermit-box-run` looked for a runner only at `agent-utils/bin/dagrun` and `agent-utils/bin/safe-ci-dag-runner`. The pinned `agent-utils` `0cdc8867` has no top-level `bin/`; `dagrun` is at `agent-utils/common/bin/dagrun`. Every invocation died with exit 2 before running anything — measured, 0 of 8 calibration seeds executed. The lookup now tries `common/bin` and `rs/bin` first, and a not-found result exits **3** rather than 2, because for a caller that is the same fact as \"this host cannot box\", and callers already branch on 3 to degrade to an announced unboxed run.\n\n**2. The calibrator and the demo disagreed about what counts as a crash.** The calibrator detects on the ASAN report text; the demo gated on exit status first. Seed 3 reports the UAF and still exits 0, and it is the lowest crashing seed here — so an ascending sweep selected exactly the seed the demo rejected as \"did not crash\". Both now use the report text, and the calibrator prefers a seed whose report reached its `SUMMARY` line, because that is the report Step 4 compares.\n\n**3. A stale seed read as a regression.** The seed is recorded as `<seed> <fixture-sha256> <hermit-sha256>` and **verified by replay** before use.\n\n### On the third field, which the owner asked about explicitly\n\nMaking the Hermit hash load-bearing is *useful but not sufficient*, and it is **not** the gate here. Measured at `00ed139b`: seeds 3, 6, 10 and 13 reproduce while 15, 17 and 19 do not, against a **fixture-identical** binary. That establishes only that *the fixture alone does not determine the seed set* — **not** that the Hermit build does. No older Hermit was built to isolate the variable, and host, kernel and toolchain were uncontrolled too. A hash gate would assume the answer to that open question, and would still vouch for a stale seed if the deciding input is one nobody hashed; it also discards good seeds whenever a release rebuild is not bit-reproducible. Replaying the seed is an *observation* rather than an inference, and holds whichever input changed. The hashes are kept because they make the recalibration reason legible.\n\n## Determinism\n\nThe demo and the calibrator were running **without `--strict`**, and that was a real defect rather than a formality. `btrfs-convert` generates a random UUID for the target filesystem, which non-strict Hermit does not virtualize:\n\n| Mode | Runs | Target UUID | UAF reproduced |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| non-strict | 3 | **two different UUIDs** | — |\n| `--strict` | 4 | `10708a9d-…` every time | **4/4** |\n\nWithin a single non-strict demo run, seed 6 reproduced the UAF at Step 2 and **missed** at Step 4, the two transcripts differing at the UUID line. Cost of `--strict` here is ~9 s per run against ~7 s. Both scripts now pass `--strict` and use one identical flag set, since a seed derived under one flag set is not evidence about another.\n\nStep 4 previously compared a four-line filtered ASAN extract, which does not contain the UUID — so it would have reported \"byte-identical\" across the two runs that actually differed. It now compares the **entire guest transcript** with only host-side lines removed: safehermit's accounting, and Hermit's own log lines, which begin with a real UTC timestamp. That is the rule the repository's comparison policy already applies to retained logs. 93 lines are compared, both UUID lines and the full ASAN report among them.\n\n## Linux Semantics\n\nNo guest-visible behaviour changes. The fixtures, the pinned btrfs-progs commit, the patch, and the observability adaptation are untouched; only which seed is selected, how it is verified, and what is compared.\n\n## Validation\n\ndevbig014, AMD EPYC 9D85. Backend **ptrace**, log level **error**, single relaxation **`--no-virtualize-cpuid`** (CPUID faulting unavailable on the demo hosts). Hermit release built at `00ed139b`, sha256 `7d559e36…`. All Hermit runs through `bin/safehermit`.\n\n- **Cold tree, no recorded seed, one command** — derives seed 6, reproduces the UAF at `task_period_wait` (`common/task-utils.c:154`) from `print_copied_inodes` (`convert/main.c:169`), fixed variant clean with the progress path engaged, replay byte-identical. **GREEN.**\n- **Stale record** (seed 17, correct fixture hash, foreign Hermit hash) — reported as `STALE SEED RECORD`, explicitly not a regression; re-derived seed 6. **GREEN.**\n- `scripts/test-prepare-demo08-calibration.sh` — **PASS**. It previously asserted on machinery `ea4840f15` had removed and exited 1 with **zero bytes of output**, so nothing it claimed had ever been checked. Six brackets now, including a stale cached seed and a truncated-vs-complete report preference.\n- `make -C demos test` — 36 passed. `./scripts/test-check-demo-review.sh` — 6 passed. `./scripts/check-checker-scheduling.rs` — OK. `shellcheck --severity=warning` clean on all six changed shell scripts.\n\nNot run here: `make lint-checks` in full, and the P0 demo gate.\n\n## Also in this change\n\n- `demos/clean.sh` is now a Demo 8 consumer — it removes the recorded seed, the one file whose staleness manufactures a false regression, and no longer exits early when the QEMU asset directory is absent.\n- `demos/run-all.sh` records a gated-out demo as `SKIP` rather than `PASS`. It still does not fail the sweep.\n- `demos/README.md` described a calibration contract the code had stopped implementing; restoring the replay makes it true again instead of deleting the promise.\n- `scripts/check-checker-scheduling.rs` allowlist reason updated to the truth. Scheduling that bracket would make the lint node depend on an ASAN runtime, because it refuses rather than skipping when it cannot build its control — that is an owner decision, left visible rather than armed unilaterally.\n","created_at":"2026-08-31T23:19:09Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T02:00:10Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/2907/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/2907/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/2907/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/statuses/68605f886745a060e0a2a8e24ab933815acc2d22","head":{"label":"rrnewton:demo-08-derive-crash-seed","ref":"demo-08-derive-crash-seed","sha":"68605f886745a060e0a2a8e24ab933815acc2d22","user":{"login":"rrnewton","id":274582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDU4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":563646124,"node_id":"R_kgDOIZiOrA","name":"hermit","full_name":"rrnewton/hermit","private":false,"owner":{"login":"rrnewton","id":274582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDU4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/gists{/gist_id}