epos/rrnewton/hermit/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/deployments","created_at":"2022-11-09T03:00:19Z","updated_at":"2026-09-17T19:31:24Z","pushed_at":"2026-09-17T19:31:22Z","git_url":"git://github.com/rrnewton/hermit.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:rrnewton/hermit.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit","homepage":null,"size":247745,"stargazers_count":1,"watchers_count":1,"language":"Rust","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":true,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":0,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":562,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":0,"open_issues":562,"watchers":1,"default_branch":"main"}},"_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/2694"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/2694"},"issue":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/2694"},"comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/2694/comments"},"review_comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/2694/comments"},"review_comment":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/comments{/number}"},"commits":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/2694/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/statuses/46670790208e71be0b1aa0e249297c0f4b38663a"}},"author_association":"OWNER","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/2368","id":4338597792,"node_id":"PR_kwDOIZiOrM8AAAABApm_oA","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/2368","diff_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/2368.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/2368.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/2368","number":2368,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Revive the reproducible OSS Buck2 build","user":{"login":"rrnewton","id":274582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDU4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"[hermit2, hermit-901, unresolved, devbig030, role=impl]\n\n## Plain Language Summary and Project Impact\n\nThis draft consolidates the surviving OSS Buck2 work into one Hermit pull request. The Hermit branch carries the BUCK files, OSS shim, pinned bootstrap, regeneration tooling, documentation, and gitlink to the revived Reverie branch at `868d46cf1d34d042da87acb6ec8a5738198041db`.\n\nThis is progress toward a reproducible alternative build, not a successful Hermit build. `//hermit-cli:hermit` does not link, and the shared action-cache benefit across worktrees has never been measured.\n\n## What works\n\n- Buck2 is pinned by the exact upstream DotSlash descriptor for release `2026-08-01`.\n- Reindeer is pinned at `e3d72748131d3a70378055f091e0647c1edad85e` and built with `nightly-2026-05-22`.\n- Dependency regeneration was run twice from absent outputs: 297 Hermit crates and 247 Reverie crates. The two generated outputs matched and both tracked lockfiles remained unchanged.\n- The build compiler used by the recorded validation is pinned to `nightly-2026-07-12`.\n- `reverie//:reverie-ptrace` builds with the pinned public Buck2 release; the current-head record is exit 0 in 19.5 seconds.\n- Hermit and Reverie now use one third-party Buck cell in the composed build, so the duplicate `serde_core-1.0.229` trait mismatch is gone.\n\n## What does not work\n\n`//hermit-cli:hermit` does not link. An earlier checkpoint progressed from the duplicate-serde failure into `detcore` and exposed approximately six stale Cargo-versus-BUCK edges across three packages. The current head fixes the newly visible undeclared `hex` and `sha2` edges and proceeds farther, but stops in `hermit-cli:libhermit`: five existing targets are missing dependency edges (`detcore_model`, `hermit_resources`, `addr2line`, `nix`, and `object`), and Buck targets do not yet exist for `reverie_kvm`, `reverie_liteinst`, or `reverie_rpc_transport`. `hermit-resources` also has no BUCK file.\n\nThe complete third-party target pattern remains diagnostic rather than green: it is red on optional `reverie-dbt-0.2` and `reverie-sabre-0.2` build-script environment plus the historical Windows-only `winapi-0.3-build-script-run` analysis exception.\n\n## Shared action cache\n\nThe cross-worktree shared action-cache benefit is the central reason to prefer Buck2 over Cargo, but it has not been measured. That measurement needs a Buck2-built Hermit binary, which this branch does not yet produce. Bootstrap and target-compatibility results do not demonstrate the payoff.\n\n## Generated aliases\n\nReindeer emits an unversioned crate alias only when `index.is_public_target` is true, which is derived from the manifest being processed; there is no configuration knob to emit the additional aliases needed by the composed Hermit/Reverie graph.\n\n`bootstrap/regenerate-rust-deps` therefore appends 14 aliases listed in the committed `shim/third-party/rust/shared-cell-aliases.txt`. Each name is resolved against the freshly generated BUCK file instead of hard-coding a versioned target. A dependency version change continues to resolve to the generated target, while a vanished crate or a newly native alias is a hard error.\n\n## Owner landing criterion\n\nThe owner said this may land immediately only if it adds build files without touching the Cargo world. Commit `e95ab8c945bcddf70ef60c931703c61170ab72ee` fails that criterion: it changes only `rust-toolchain.toml`, pinning `nightly` to `nightly-2026-07-12` and adding the `clippy` and `rustfmt` components.\n\nThat commit is mechanically separable: it modifies one file, and no later commit touches `rust-toolchain.toml`. It was not split here. Removing it would restore a floating compiler and fail the cold-reviewer reproducibility requirement, so whether to separate it is an owner decision.\n\n## Known review boundaries\n\n- Hermit is `26276e2b266e944bc02ff775b4ceb5cb0956019e`; the draft was opened without rebasing, as requested, and is five commits behind `rrnewton/hermit:main` at `d252f99acb2d790cc2f6ad2a2ed8c1c85d9ef7f7`.\n- The gitlink uses revived Reverie `868d46cf1d34d042da87acb6ec8a5738198041db`, while `.gitmodules` still names the older `buck2` branch for `--remote` updates. Ordinary recursive checkout uses the exact gitlink; `git submodule update --remote reverie` would not.\n- Hermit Cargo manifests and lockfiles still pin Reverie main `f2e9839e5316e31c377089ae7f789515ba9d2550`; the Buck source cell uses `868d46cf`. The PR does not claim those two build paths use identical Reverie source.\n- Public DotSlash 0.5.9 was used for the recorded pinned-Buck2 validation. This host internal `/usr/bin/dotslash` rejects the public descriptor with `missing field scheme`; `docs/BUCK2_OSS.md` records the public-reviewer command and the exact divergence.\n\n## Determinism\n\nThe regeneration check compares two independently generated BUCK outputs and rejects lockfile changes. No Hermit execution assurance level is claimed because this branch does not produce a Hermit binary.\n\n## Validation\n\nRecorded on the branch at the named commits, using public DotSlash 0.5.9, Buck2 release `2026-08-01`, and toolchain `nightly-2026-07-12`:\n\n- `bootstrap/regenerate-rust-deps`: exit 0; 297 Hermit crates and 247 Reverie crates; repeated generated outputs matched; both lockfiles unchanged.\n- `bootstrap/buck2 build reverie//:reverie-ptrace`: exit 0 in 19.5 seconds at current head.\n- `bootstrap/buck2 build --keep-going shim//third-party/rust/...`: expected diagnostic red described above; 14 incompatible targets skipped under the pinned release.\n- `bootstrap/buck2 build //hermit-cli:hermit`: fails at the missing first-party edges and targets listed above; no binary produced.\n\nThis consolidation action did not rerun builds or alter either pushed branch.\n\nTask: consolidate-buck2-onto-one-pr","created_at":"2026-08-22T14:32:57Z","updated_at":"2026-08-25T20:21:21Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/2368/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/2368/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/2368/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/statuses/26276e2b266e944bc02ff775b4ceb5cb0956019e","head":{"label":"rrnewton:revive/buck2-oss-901","ref":"revive/buck2-oss-901","sha":"26276e2b266e944bc02ff775b4ceb5cb0956019e","user":{"login":"rrnewton","id":274582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDU4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":563646124,"node_id":"R_kgDOIZiOrA","name":"hermit","full_name":"rrnewton/hermit","private":false,"owner":{"login":"rrnewton","id":274582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDU4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit","description":"Hermit launches linux x86_64 programs in a special, hermetically isolated sandbox to control their execution. Hermit translates normal, nondeterministic behavior, into deterministic, repeatable behavior. This can be used for various applications, including replay-debugging, reproducible artifacts, chaos mode concurrency testing and bug analysis.","fork":true,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit","forks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/forks","keys_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/keys{/key_id}","collaborators_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/collaborators{/collaborator}","teams_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/teams","hooks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/hooks","issue_events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/events{/number}","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/events","assignees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/assignees{/user}","branches_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/branches{/branch}","tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/tags","blobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/git/blobs{/sha}","git_tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/git/tags{/sha}","git_refs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/git/refs{/sha}","trees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/git/trees{/sha}","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/statuses/{sha}","languages_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/languages","stargazers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/stargazers","contributors_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/subscrib